# PRD documentation sync

`PRD.md` (repo root) is the **master product requirements document**. Do not create a competing PRD file.

When a user-facing feature, detection rule, escalation ladder, data-model summary, or demo path changes materially:

1. Update the relevant section(s) of **`PRD.md`**.
2. Bump the **Last updated** date in the header table.
3. Point detailed schema / API / design specifics at `docs/DATABASE.md`, `docs/API.md`, and `docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md` rather than duplicating long tables.

Keep safety invariants (presence / left-behind / heat / buckle) accurate to the implemented code (`SeatStatus`, `AlertService`, firmware thresholds).
